  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41123-PROJECT-240034</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and youth entrepreneurship in western Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ongoing crisis in Ukraine has the largest impact on vulnerable communities, including youth, women and internally displaced persons (IDPs). Economic disruption, combined with massive internal displacement and refugee flows have been causing significant declines in employment and income. Within the umbrella of UNIDO#s green industrial recovery programme for Ukraine 2024-2028, the development objective of the project is to foster self-employment opportunities for youth and women in a selected region (oblast) of western Ukraine. The project aims at increased economic engagement and income-generating opportunities for youth and women through technical support at the meso- and micro levels. Meso-level interventions will focus on strengthening the capacity and knowledge of selected entrepreneurial support structures serving youth and women, including IDPs, in the domains of innovative entrepreneurship, digitalization and supply chain development and m anagement. Micro-level interventions will entail assistance to women, youth and IDPs through entrepreneurial training and business coaching to facilitate the development of business plans and the launch of entrepreneurial activities in one region (oblast) to be selected at the outset of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
